GR4H Vibe Lab — dashboard design (Pencil pass)

Design canvas: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/92214579-c2b9-4395-bd16-b10937ff072a
Working source (edit these, not the published file directly): design/pencil/Main.dc.html, design/pencil/Mobile.dc.html, design/pencil/canvas.json

Status: static review mockup, not yet wired to app code. app/page.tsx is
still the empty scaffold from the earlier prompts.

Two frames:
- Main (1440x960, desktop): header, ~300px left parameter panel
  ("Experiment Controls" > Catchment / Model Parameters / Initial
  Condition + Reset), then main column in this order: Hydrograph (big,
  first) -> 4 KPI cards -> x4 sensitivity experiment (chart + Case/Peak
  Q/Lag table) -> "What changed?" insight card. A small dark arrow badge
  sits on the panel/content divider to cue controls -> response.
- Mobile: header, a COLLAPSED "Experiment Controls" card (one-line
  tabular summary, chevron), then the same Hydrograph -> KPI -> Sensitivity
  -> Insight order as desktop, so the hydrograph reads first on both
  breakpoints.

Revision (review pass against 8 criteria: hydrograph-first, control/result
causality, x1-x4 legibility, axis confusion, rain-vs-flow-peak distinction,
projector readability, cross-breakpoint hierarchy, decoration audit):
- Reordered main column so Hydrograph leads (was below the KPI row);
  KPIs now read as the quantified follow-up, not the headline.
- Added a panel title "Experiment Controls" + a connector arrow badge at
  the panel/content boundary, and a "Model response to the controls at
  left" caption under the Hydrograph title, to make the causal link explicit.
- Bumped x1-x4 name weight (now bold, not muted) and slider font 13->14px.
- Every chart axis tick now carries its unit (incl. both "0" baselines:
  "0 mm/h" vs "0 m³/s") so the precip/flow axes can't be confused.
- Rain Peak and Q Peak markers are now differentiated by dash pattern,
  line weight, badge position (rain peak badge sits in the precip zone,
  Q peak badge in the flow zone), and each has its own colored dot
  marker on its actual data point rather than two look-alike gray lines.
- Global type bump for projector legibility: chart axis/legend text
  10-11px -> 12px (14px on the smaller mobile frame), darkened the muted
  text color from #71716c to #5c5c58 for better contrast at a distance.
- Mobile "Experiment Controls" card is now collapsed by default (was
  fully expanded), so the hydrograph appears near the top of the scroll
  on mobile too, matching desktop's hierarchy.
- Card-count audit: no redundant/decorative cards found; none removed.

Every number and curve on the canvas was generated by actually running
lib/gr4h.ts + lib/storm.ts + lib/metrics.ts (buildScenarioInput() default
scenario, 72h) — not fabricated placeholder data. Slider fill positions
match lib/storm.ts PARAMETER_RANGES exactly.

Known gap to resolve when this becomes code: the design shows a PET
slider under "Catchment" (per the Prompt 5 brief), but PET is not in
PARAMETER_RANGES / ScenarioOverrides in lib/storm.ts (Prompt 4 fixed PET
at 0.1 mm/h, not user-adjustable). Decide whether to add PET to
lib/storm.ts's adjustable set or drop the slider before wiring the UI.
